         pkexec,
         polkitd
Description: settings only the DragonBox Pyra has
 Pyra Settings is a small GTK 3 app for the Pyra's own settings. Version 1
 covers suspend and wake: which game buttons and whether the lid wake the
 machine, and what the lid, idle sleep and a critical battery do.
 .
 Wake settings go through a pkexec helper that writes only known sysfs files
 and keeps them in /etc/pyra-settings/pyra-settings.conf, which
 pyra-settings-apply.service reapplies at boot.
